*.rej
*.pid
*.seed

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 10. GENERATED SYNTHETIC DATA  (regenerable — see justification)
#
# WHY EXCLUDED (this is a hygiene decision, not a blanket directory ignore):
#   - generated/ is 584 MB in total.
#   - THREE files exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit and would cause the push
#     to be REJECTED outright:
#         usage_daily      146 MB
#         payments         120 MB
#         bill_line_items  104 MB
#     Two more exceed the 50 MB warning threshold (billing 86 MB,
#     network_events 71 MB).
#   - The data is FULLY REPRODUCIBLE from committed code:
#     ingestion/synthetic_data_gen/config.py defaults RANDOM_SEED to 42, so
#     `python -m ingestion.synthetic_data_gen.main` regenerates byte-identical
#     output on any clone. Nothing is lost by excluding it.
#
# The two tiny reference datasets are deliberately KEPT so reviewers can still
# inspect the real output format without downloading 584 MB.
# (If you later want the full data in the repo, use Git LFS rather than
#  removing these rules.)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
generated/**/*.parquet
!generated/plans/*.parquet
!generated/promotions/*.parquet

# Other bulk data formats, wherever they appear
*.avro
*.orc
*.tfrecord

# Local database files
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.duckdb

# NOTE: .csv, .md, .yaml, .yml, .sqlx, .json, .parquet are NOT blanket-ignored.
# Project configuration (dataform.json, package.json), all SQLX definitions,
# all Markdown documentation, and the two sample parquet files remain tracked.
